      "problem": "Which of the following is a type II region in two-dimensional space?",
      "worked_solution": "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14114484/assets/7c159c025f0b7ae4bfa8984f637a492cda21ec2dd39e87be724324e1334c06a3.png)",
